<p>I appreciate you taking the time to read my article and leave your thoughts! I guess I'll say a few things:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">No&nbsp;more&nbsp;stuff?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>A feather tickling device to make the president scratch his nose in his sleep?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If it works, it works. ¯\_(ツ)_/¯</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Furthermore, for me to accept the world of this article, I have to decide that, not only is the president kept in the dark about the Foundation for some reason</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, so, (in my headcanon at least), the foundation CANNOT tell elected officials about the veil or the anomalous. What if Trump wakes up one day and decides to tweet about the aliens? What if Bernie Sanders decides to tell the world about their D Class experiments? The veil is fragile, and they can't risk giving information to anyone aside from their most trusted.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Foundation agents somehow both casually stroll into the White House in one event while rooftop snipers start shooting at them in another, which shows off the lack of even internal consistency.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, these were two entirely different situations. The first situation was just an ordinary day with ordinary security. In the second one, they were on extremely high security. The White House was barricaded, and the President was escorted to a secure bunker that's literally designed to <a target="_blank" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presidential_Emergency_Operations_Center">protect the president</a> from an aerial attack on Washington.</p>
<p>Despite having SS credentials, they were denied access and had to forcefully bypass the police line. When they literally beat their way through, the WH assumed they were being attacked by some kind of paramilitary organization, hence the response. (And as stated, their communications were jammed by agents embedded in the WH)</p>
